     9	
    10	- **Tables beside the ontology.** `gnd export ossie` now writes five files.
    11	  The two new ones are `OUT.semantic_model.<fmt>`, the tables that hold the
    12	  model's facts, and `OUT.mapping.<fmt>`, which says where each concept and
    13	  relationship is stored. The ontology, sidecar and loss report keep their
    14	  bytes. A file already at either new path stops the run with exit
    15	  11 (`EXIT_COLLISION`) and nothing is written. `--ontology-only` keeps the
    16	  three-file run. A model that yields no table writes three files and a note.
    17	- **Your own tables.** `--physical-binding FILE` describes delivered tables
    18	  in place of the generated ones. The file follows the packaged schema
    19	  `gnd-physical-binding/1`. A binding the model contradicts is refused with
    20	  a `binding:` rule id and exit 3. Together with `--ontology-only` it is a
    21	  usage error, exit 64 (`EXIT_USAGE`). A fact that a table holds only
    22	  through a surrogate key cannot be bound; it is listed as `unbound`.
    23	- **Larger files.** `--max-output-bytes N` on `gnd export ossie` and
    24	  `--max-input-bytes N` on `gnd import ossie` raise the 10 MiB bound for one
    25	  run, up to 256 MiB. A value outside that range is a usage error, exit
    26	  64 (`EXIT_USAGE`). The model file itself stays capped at 10 MiB.
    27	- **Where to read more.** [Ossie interchange in GND](explanation/ossie.md)
    28	  and [Describe your delivered tables](how-to/describe-delivered-tables-for-ossie.md).
